{
  "description": "A compatibility-preserving diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec. DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returns metrics and metric_definitions derived from the trained recommender and available public data. Probes must remain valid when the architecture changes.",
  "motivation": "Support model diagnosis and iterative improvement while preserving the benchmark contract, preventing unsupported behavioral claims, and selecting models using comparable validation results.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain the required class and method signatures. Access the actual trained module through view.model and maintain or adapt view.item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data. Batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L. Use only interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; mark unavailable information as unobserved. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for 20 real training users, five per category. Preserve all four datasets and routing. Select models by macro-average validation HR@10 under the pinned evaluator; diagnostic metrics are supplementary. Architecture changes must also update the predictor writer.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    init(view, device): store view and device\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        save model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        without gradients:\n            inspect batches through architecture-compatible view methods\n            compute diagnostics supported by observed data\n            attach definitions and availability information\n        restore model training state\n        return metrics, metric_definitions\n\nFor each category:\n    generate full-catalog recommendations excluding seen items\n    for five selected real training users\nEvaluate candidate models using pinned validation HR@10\nSelect using the mean HR@10 across all four categories",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines architecture-aware diagnostics with explicit data-availability constraints and a shared evaluation contract.",
    "negative": "Primarily an integration specification; it introduces no new recommendation algorithm or diagnostic estimator."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support comparable diagnostics across model architectures and guide targeted improvements.",
    "negative": "Its value depends on the diagnostic measures implemented and whether they predict validation improvements; neither is established here."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The fixed interface and batch shapes make the adapter straightforward to integrate with SASRec.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require careful compatibility updates, and full-catalog scoring must handle memory use, item routing, and seen-item exclusion."
  }
}
